I've just now made another change to my patch:
* Reading coins now works when GOLDOBJ is set.

Also, I noticed some similarity in my coin-reading code and some code
(or the lack thereof) in the Coin Flipping patch by Pasi Kallinen.
(Specifically, it relates to getobj() and its capriciousness.) Now, I'd
been meaning on doing a bugfix update to that patch, so I decided to
merge this and my patch together. I then made the following
improvements to the Coin Flipping patch:
* Handling when you flip coins over water, lava, pits, holes and on the
Air level.
* Coins are no longer prompted in the "What do you want to use or
apply" prompt.
* There is now a 1 in 1000000 chance of the flipped coin landing on its
edge - but obviously only if the coin falls on the ground.


